fix: hero shows the real product, and diagrams match the app's palette

The landing was promising something the demo did not deliver, and it led with
the wrong thing.

Positioning: notes are the product; study mode is a feature for students. The
hero led with the tutor, which narrowed the whole pitch. Now the headline and
demo are about the note loop, and study mode has a proper feature card (it had
none) alongside the other nine.

Hero demo now shows what the app actually does: type a note, type [[ to open
the note picker, the link completes and a backlink appears on the other note.
That is the real core loop rather than an idealised mockup.

Also fixed:
- the old static app preview still said "second-brain" — stale branding on a
  live page, missed because the rename was case-sensitive. Removed the whole
  mockup: it was redundant next to the live demo and showed a UI that no
  longer matches the app.
- a chart label was clipping outside its viewBox.
- Mermaid diagrams rendered with a clashing red/maroon rainbow because the
  cScale palette was never overridden, so the app looked worse than the
  landing claimed. Whole ramp is now brand purple in both themes.
